TIP:  The (A) (Asus4) (A) (Asus2) permeates the song but is easy to play and is all on/offs.  Play (A) with your middle three fingers, then add your pinky to the 2nd string/3rd fret for (Asus4), then lift your pinky to get back to (A), lift off the bottom/ring finger to get to (Asus2), and replace to get back to (A).  Easy as Sunday morning but the sequence moves quickly so don't dawdle.  Note during the verse the first (A) in the sequence starts with the last word of the line.


